  "details": "Now that vrchat has groups, I think a good feature would be an audio block. \n\nThe default block which hides the affected user and stops audio works well if you don't want to interact with a user again. \n\nHOWEVER: This default block is not good if you're in a vrchat group. In vrchat groups you often *have* to continue partially interacting with the other user.\n\nThe default block leads to unnecessary awkward situations:\n\n-you still need to see the affected person to do things like group photos. \n\n-an invisible blocked user is standing in the same place as another user\n\n-both users try to change map options or related\n\nAt the same time, muting is not enough. The muted person can still hear what you are saying.\n\nI propose vrchat: \n\n***add an audio block that blocks the mic and user voice of the affected person, \n\n*but also* stops the other person from hearing you.\n\nI also think this would be an easy feature to implement with Unity.\n\nI think this feature will make vrchat public and vrchat groups better.",
